{"repositoryId":963116751,"availability":"available","full":"felixpalmer/a5","name":"a5","description":"Pentagonal geospatial indexing system DGGS","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":332,"forks":13,"created":"2025-04-09T07:23:00Z","updated":"2026-10-15T21:11:55Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://a5geo.org","topics":["a5","data-science","data-visualization","deck-gl","dggs","discrete-global-grid-system","gis","map-visualization","maps","visualization"],"demo":"https://a5geo.org/examples/duckdb-playground","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.428Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.428Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.428Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.428Z","stars":332,"forks":13}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A5 is a geospatial index that partitions the world into pentagonal cells. The cells are available at 31 resolution levels, from a handful covering the whole world down to less than 30mm², and every cell at a given resolution has exactly the same area. Each cell is identified by a 64-bit integer, which is frozen from v1.0: an A5 cell ID stored today will refer to the same place in the future.","Once data is in cells, very different datasets can be joined, aggregated and compared directly: points can be counted per cell, as with the density of holiday rentals across a city, and regions such as countries or parcels of land become coverings, sets of cells which support union, intersection and difference."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/felixpalmer/a5/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9d5008ca560dcac01e88aa6340972b8c159463da8140a4a483542f19425b05a9","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.616Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:58.616Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A5 is a geospatial index that partitions the world into pentagonal cells. The cells are available at 31 resolution levels, f